WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.370
Above a forest, a mast samples the air.

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.170
Its CO₂ readings swing
between day and night.

3
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:12.010
Since 1958, CO₂ has been
measured at Mauna Loa in Hawaiʻi,

4
00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:15.630
on bare lava with no vegetation or soil.

5
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:22.730
In September 2026, the monthly
mean: 426.07 parts per million.

6
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:28.210
One ice core holds bubbles of
past air going back 800,000 years.

7
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:33.830
With the air swinging every day, how do
scientists spot the slow change underneath?

8
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.990
In this mission, you'll
compare change over a day,

9
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.550
a year and millions of years.

10
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.170
Then you'll meet the tools
that monitor water and carbon.

11
00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:48.590
Your mission: find out how scientists
separate slow change from natural swings.
